newlib-guest.patch: the two rules by which newlib is built for the guest (fnv-nx, L2 lead rulings 2026-11-15). Apply with patch -p0 from the
directory that holds newlib-4.6.0.20260123/ (after the devkitPro patch and the L5 patches).

NL-LDBL: newlib's libm/ld and libm/ld128 are the `*l` functions of a long double that is NOT double (libm/ld/fpmath.h and invtrig.h know
LDBL_MANT_DIG 64 and 113 only). They are built iff newlib's own configure test says so: newlib_cv_ldbl_eq_dbl (configure.ac, "whether long
double equals double") is not `yes`. The guest compiler's long double is binary64 (msvcmodel, LDBL_MANT_DIG 53), the test gives
newlib_cv_ldbl_eq_dbl=yes in the ilp32 multilib (b-newlib/.../config.log), and the `*l` functions of that case are the _LDBL_EQ_DBL alias
blocks of libm/common/*.c. No file list: one AM_CONDITIONAL on the configure result. configure and Makefile.in are regenerated by the
autotools versions the tarball's own files state (autoconf 2.69, automake 1.15.1), which reproduce the tarball's configure and Makefile.in
byte for byte before this patch (checked by build.sh).

NL-SECT: the flags of every runtime compile come from one record, guest_compiler.json (the semantic flags and runtime_cflags). newlib's
configure.host adds a second source for aarch64 (`newlib_cflags` -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections), which splits every object's code and
data into per-symbol sections; that line is removed. (configure.host is read by configure: nothing is regenerated.)
--- newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/configure.ac
+++ newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/configure.ac
@@ -723,6 +723,9 @@
 if test $newlib_cv_ldbl_eq_dbl = yes; then
   AC_DEFINE(_LDBL_EQ_DBL, 1, [Define if the platform long double type is equal to double.])
 fi
+dnl fnv-nx NL-LDBL: libm/ld and libm/ld128 hold the long double functions of a long double that is NOT double (binary80 / binary128: LDBL_MANT_DIG 64 or 113);
+dnl they are built iff the configure test above says long double differs from double.
+AM_CONDITIONAL(LDBL_NE_DBL, test x"$newlib_cv_ldbl_eq_dbl" != x"yes")
 
 AC_CONFIG_FILES([Makefile])
 AC_OUTPUT
--- newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/libm/Makefile.inc
+++ newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/libm/Makefile.inc
@@ -46,7 +46,9 @@
 include %D%/common/Makefile.inc
 
 if HAVE_FPMATH_H
+if LDBL_NE_DBL
 include %D%/ld/Makefile.inc
+endif # LDBL_NE_DBL
 endif # HAVE_FPMATH_H
 
 include %D%/complex/Makefile.inc
@@ -55,7 +57,9 @@
 
 if HAVE_LIBM_MACHINE_AARCH64
 include %D%/machine/aarch64/Makefile.inc
+if LDBL_NE_DBL
 include %D%/ld128/Makefile.inc
+endif # LDBL_NE_DBL
 endif
 if HAVE_LIBM_MACHINE_AMDGCN
 include %D%/machine/amdgcn/Makefile.inc
@@ -87,7 +91,9 @@
 endif
 if HAVE_LIBM_MACHINE_RISCV
 include %D%/machine/riscv/Makefile.inc
+if LDBL_NE_DBL
 include %D%/ld128/Makefile.inc
+endif # LDBL_NE_DBL
 endif
 if HAVE_LIBM_MACHINE_X86_64
 include %D%/machine/x86_64/Makefile.inc
--- newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/configure.host
+++ newlib-4.6.0.20260123/newlib/configure.host
@@ -644,7 +644,6 @@
 	default_newlib_io_long_long="yes"
 	default_newlib_io_pos_args="yes"
 	newlib_cflags="${newlib_cflags} -D__DYNAMIC_REENT__  -DGETREENT_PROVIDED -DREENTRANT_SYSCALLS_PROVIDED -D__DEFAULT_UTF8__"
-	newlib_cflags="${newlib_cflags} -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections"
 	syscall_dir=syscalls
 	;;
   arc*-*-*)
